{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02229",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.16,
      "end_seconds": 4.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "hello, sorry about the delay, do sit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.57,
      "end_seconds": 9.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Hello. I hope I'm not late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.03,
      "end_seconds": 20.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Doctor, um, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.55,
      "end_seconds": 26.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome. Tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 27.81,
      "end_seconds": 33.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "We came cos of a chronic cough with lots of phlegm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.86,
      "end_seconds": 37.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.28,
      "end_seconds": 41.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "about three weeks, give or take"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 42.43,
      "end_seconds": 46.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "It was closer to a month, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.3,
      "end_seconds": 53.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.95,
      "end_seconds": 55.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Yes, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.85,
      "end_seconds": 62.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.28,
      "end_seconds": 73.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "It's severe, honestly. It happens on and off. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.89,
      "end_seconds": 81.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 81.19,
      "end_seconds": 87.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "So, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.34,
      "end_seconds": 99.22,
      "duration_seconds": 10.88,
      "text": "Yeah, I was getting to that! I've also been getting out of breath. I've also had green phlegm lately, since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 100.58,
      "end_seconds": 104.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Yes, that's right, that's how it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.44,
      "end_seconds": 108.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.39,
      "end_seconds": 113.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Mm, I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 117.22,
      "end_seconds": 123.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Hold on, doctor, I think she reacted to naproxen once. I'm not certain, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.03,
      "end_seconds": 127.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "I don't remember that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.92,
      "end_seconds": 136.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.32,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.75,
      "end_seconds": 142.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Yes, I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder, two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.1,
      "end_seconds": 149.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.72,
      "end_seconds": 159.03,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "I take omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day. I take hydrocortisone cream, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.11,
      "end_seconds": 165.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.98,
      "end_seconds": 174.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "yes, migraines. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.51,
      "end_seconds": 176.21,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.97,
      "end_seconds": 184.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Yes, acid reflux. I kept putting it it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.92,
      "end_seconds": 190.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "is that everything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.75,
      "end_seconds": 204.32,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "Eczema, for five years. My neighbour said I should get it looked at. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know. I've had depression, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.86,
      "end_seconds": 214.86,
      "duration_seconds": 10.0,
      "text": "Right, right. Okay, I can see acid reflux and eczema in your file as well. Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.6,
      "end_seconds": 218.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.21,
      "end_seconds": 220.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.69,
      "end_seconds": 228.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.88,
      "end_seconds": 232.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.26,
      "end_seconds": 238.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.0,
      "end_seconds": 241.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.22,
      "end_seconds": 247.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.91,
      "end_seconds": 252.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Any chest pain or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.79,
      "end_seconds": 263.98,
      "duration_seconds": 10.19,
      "text": "No, no chest pain, no coughing up blood. I did have tiredness at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.55,
      "end_seconds": 269.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Have you noticed fever or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.89,
      "end_seconds": 273.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "no, none that I've noticed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.76,
      "end_seconds": 278.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "what about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.22,
      "end_seconds": 283.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "No, um, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 287.52,
      "end_seconds": 296.71,
      "duration_seconds": 9.19,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temperature 36.7, BP is 126 over 77, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, respiratory rate 18, pulse 65."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.23,
      "end_seconds": 302.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.83,
      "end_seconds": 307.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.01,
      "end_seconds": 310.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "let me feel here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.99,
      "end_seconds": 333.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "There are coarse crackles at both bases and the fingers are slightly clubbed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.81,
      "end_seconds": 340.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "thank you, you can get dressed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.73,
      "end_seconds": 368.2,
      "duration_seconds": 12.47,
      "text": "let me tell you where I've got to. It's hard to say. A flare of bronchiectasis is one possibility and a chest infection another, and I'd rather not commit yet"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 369.97,
      "end_seconds": 372.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.7,
      "end_seconds": 383.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.75,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a flare of bronchiectasis is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.79,
      "end_seconds": 397.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Let's book a chest X-ray to to look into bronchiectasis flare."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.49,
      "end_seconds": 403.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Okay, so how long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.88,
      "end_seconds": 431.97,
      "duration_seconds": 28.09,
      "text": "I'm sending you for a sputum culture cos of purulent sputum we'll begin with clarithromycin, 500 milligrams, twice a day, fourteen days that should help with bronchiectasis flare keep up your airway clearance exercises twice a day let's get you seen by the the respiratory clinic, I'll arrange the letter please don't wait if the symptoms get worse that's when to be seen urgently let's plan a check in two weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.94,
      "end_seconds": 434.64,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 436.41,
      "end_seconds": 439.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "So, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 441.28,
      "end_seconds": 444.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Okay, so alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 445.34,
      "end_seconds": 446.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}